More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (371–380)
371. Improper Security Headers
Missing Security Headers
Web applications lack important HTTP security headers such as CSP, HSTS, or X-Frame-Options.
💰 Typical payout: $100 – $2,000
372. Sensitive Data in URL Parameters
Sensitive Data Exposure in URL
Sensitive information like tokens or IDs is passed in URLs and may leak through logs or browser history.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
373. Improper Authorization on API Endpoints
API Authorization Bypass
APIs allow users to access resources belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
374. Open Port Exposure
Open Port Misconfiguration
Unnecessary ports are exposed to the internet, potentially revealing internal services.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
375. Insecure Cookie Domain Scope
Cookie Domain Scope Misconfiguration
Cookies are accessible across multiple subdomains, increasing the risk of session theft.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
376. Insecure Default Credentials
Default Credential Vulnerability
Applications or services use default usernames and passwords that attackers can guess.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $6,000
377. Improper Logout Functionality
Session Logout Vulnerability
Users remain authenticated even after logging out due to session mismanagement.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
378. Insecure File Metadata Exposure
File Metadata Information Disclosure
Documents reveal internal data like usernames, system paths, or software versions.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
379. Unprotected Admin Panels
Admin Panel Exposure
Administrative dashboards are accessible without proper authentication.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
380. Improper Session Timeout
Session Timeout Misconfiguration
Sessions remain active for too long, increasing the risk of unauthorized access.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
